---
epr-meta-version: 1
id: experience-stories-governance
covers: subtree
purpose: >
  The canonical experience-story catalog — plain-language narratives, one per (subject, role, feature)
  triple, that a reader who has never read a spec should recognize themselves in. Every story write
  carries a context-blind reader review, so the story stands without the session that wrote it.
rules:
  - id: experience-story-blind-reader-review
    class: inject
    when: { write: "*--*--*.md" }
    route-to: { dest: blind-reader }
    parameters:
      review-profile: experience-story
      variance:
        floor: one considered fresh read; fix its correctness findings; close by the author's judgment
        requires: steward-of-record
        offered-when: the session's declared purpose is authoring the stories in scope
    why: >
      After the authoring pass, dispatch a fresh-context blind-reader with ONLY the completed story
      path and the `experience-story` review profile. Do not provide the conversation, plan, persona
      records, feature files, epics, or an explanation of what the author meant. Revise from its
      findings, then repeat with a new blind reader until the story is READY or the operator explicitly
      defers named findings.
      Each finding carries a class (correctness | interpretability | preference); the loop closes when a
      fresh reader returns no correctness or interpretability finding, and preference findings never
      reopen it. Record the loop's cost where the work already reports — the commit message or the
      owning habit delta — as rounds, per-class counts per round, and findings resolved. Every round
      still uses a new reader.
      The loop is owed when the writer's attention is elsewhere — a technical run that touches a story
      in passing. A session whose declared purpose is the story itself discharges it at the `variance`
      floor above, and only under a session-covenant clause the steward of record granted for that
      session and those paths (`epr covenant`); an agent never grants itself the floor.
---
# genesis/data/stories — the canonical experience-story catalog

Schema, voice and lifecycle live in `CONVENTIONS.md`; the storyteller agent owns the directory.

## The review gate

`experience-story-blind-reader-review` matches the triple filename
(`<subject>--<role>--<feature>.md`), so `CONVENTIONS.md`, `INDEX.md` and the one retired
pre-triple story are not story writes. It is the same rule the a2o stories carry
(`genesis/a2o/.epr-meta`), with a profile for prose instead of Gherkin: a fresh reader receives
only the story path and reports whether a stranger can recover who the story is about, what they
went through, and why it mattered, without the persona records, features or epics the story was
composed from.

The full loop is the default. The `variance` floor applies only under a covenant clause the steward
of record grants for a session whose declared purpose is writing these stories.
